T* () Tj
T* (1 Purpose and scope) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (1.1 Purpose) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Admins import customers from a CSV file instead of entering them one by one. Sales teams) Tj
T* (often receive customer lists from events and partners, and typing hundreds of records by) Tj
T* (hand is slow and error prone.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (1.2 Goals) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (- An admin can import a list of up to several thousand customers in one go.) Tj
T* (- Rows that cannot be imported are reported with a reason, so the admin can fix them and) Tj
T* (try again.) Tj
T* (- Nothing is imported until the admin has seen a preview and confirmed it.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (1.3 In scope) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (- Uploading one CSV file at a time from the Customers page.) Tj
T* (- Mapping the file's columns to customer fields.) Tj
T* (- Validating every row before anything is written.) Tj
T* (- A preview, the import itself, a summary and a downloadable error report.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (1.4 Out of scope) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (- Importing from Excel files or from other systems through an API.) Tj
T* (- Updating customers in bulk by any other means.) Tj
T* (- Scheduled or recurring imports.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (2 Users and permissions) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Only admins can import customers. The Import button is shown on the Customers page to) Tj
T* (admins only.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (An admin can see the imports they started and their error reports.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (3 Uploading a file) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (3.1 Choosing a file) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The admin opens the Customers page, selects Import and chooses a file from their computer,) Tj
T* (or drags the file onto the upload area.) Tj
