(Files must be CSV files encoded in UTF-8. A comma separates the values, and a value that) Tj
T* (contains a comma is wrapped in double quotes.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (3.2 Limits) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Files are limited to 10,000 rows.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The maximum file size is 5 MB.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (A file over either limit is rejected before it is uploaded, with a message that names the) Tj
T* (limit.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Large files should import quickly.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (3.3 Progress) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (While the file uploads, the page shows a progress bar with the percentage sent.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (4 Mapping columns) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (4.1 Headers) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The first row of the file holds the column headers. The importer reads the headers and) Tj
T* (suggests a customer field for each one by its name.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (4.2 Accepted columns) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The accepted columns are Email, Name, Phone, Company, Date of birth, etc.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Each customer field can be mapped to at most one column. A column the admin does not map) Tj
T* (is ignored.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (4.3 Saving a mapping) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The admin can save a mapping and choose it again for the next import from the same source.) Tj
T* () Tj
